
Note:  The rupee symbol occupies three bytes in UTF-8, but it is one character.
=====
wc -c counts the size of the encoded data in bytes
wc -m counts characters according to the current locale


wc filename  --> to know no of lines, words, bytes in file


wc -l filename  --> lines


wc -w filename  --> words


wc -m file      --> Characters


wc -c filename  --> bytes


wc -L sample.txt   --> Finds the longest line


ls -l | wc -l   --> no of files & directories (1 less)


ls -l | grep "drwx*" | wc -l   --> no of dirctores


grep word filename | wc -l   --> no of lines contains word


sort names.txt | uniq | wc -l     --> Count unique lines


